// self-hosted::hlir — High-Level Intermediate Representation (SSA form)
//
// This module provides the HLIR data structures and lowering pass
// that bridges the gap between the type-checked AST and the codegen backends.
//
// HLIR is consumed by:
//   - LLVM codegen  (self-hosted/llvm/codegen.sio)
//   - GPU codegen   (self-hosted/gpu/hlir_to_gpu.sio)
//   - Native codegen can also consume HLIR via self-hosted/native/lower_hir.sio
//
// Architecture:
//   Source -> Lexer -> Parser -> AST -> Check -> [HIR] -> HLIR -> Backend
//
// Files in this module:
//   ir.sio          — Data structures (HlirModule, HlirFunction, HlirBlock, etc.)
//   builder.sio     — FunctionBuilder for constructing HLIR (SSA construction)
//   lower.sio       — AST/HIR -> HLIR lowering
//   lower_effects.sio — Effect handler lowering to HLIR
//   opt_strategy.sio — Strategy-directed optimization passes
//
// The HLIR is an SSA-form IR with:
//   - Basic blocks with phi nodes
//   - Explicit terminators (branch, cond_branch, switch, return)
//   - Typed instructions (every value has a known HlirType)
//   - Effect dispatch operations
//   - Full type coverage (primitives, aggregates, hypercomplex, epistemic)

// Re-export all public items from submodules
pub use ir::*
pub use builder::*
pub use lower::*
pub use opt_strategy::*
